{number: 40}
{title: Glory to His Name}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Down at the cross where my Savior died,
Down where for cleansing from [G7] sin I cried,
[C] There to my heart was the [F] blood applied;
[C] Glory to [G7] His [C] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Glory to His name, [F] glory to His [C] name;
There to my heart was the [F] blood applied;
[C] Glory to [G7] His [C] name!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] I am so wondrously saved from sin,
Jesus so sweetly a-[G7] bides within,
[C] There at the cross where He [F] took me in;
[C] Glory to [G7] His [C] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
O [C] precious fountain that saves from sin,
I am so glad I have [G7] entered in;
[C] There Jesus saves me and [F] keeps me clean;
[C] Glory to [G7] His [C] name!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Come to this fountain so rich and sweet;
Cast your poor soul at the [G7] Savior’s feet;
[C] Plunge in today and be [F] made complete;
[C] Glory to [G7] His [C] name!
{end_of_verse}
